1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,220
Describe a part in your own words, and SOMA AI builds it as a real 3D model.

2
00:00:08,303 --> 00:00:11,393
No CAD knowledge needed, and you never have to touch the code.

3
00:00:15,978 --> 00:00:20,586
SOMA is a free, open-source desktop app for designing 3D parts with AI.

4
00:00:20,586 --> 00:00:23,312
Its own agent, SOMA AI, is built right in.

5
00:00:23,312 --> 00:00:29,868
You describe what you need, SOMA AI writes the model as code, and SOMA builds it and shows it to you.

6
00:00:30,568 --> 00:00:36,378
In this tutorial, we go from installing SOMA to a finished part, and then look at the tools that help you get it right.

7
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:38,745
Get SOMA from somacad.app.

8
00:00:38,745 --> 00:00:42,462
The download page picks the right package for your system:

9
00:00:42,462 --> 00:00:48,488
an installer or a portable ZIP for Windows, a disk image for macOS, and an AppImage for Linux.

10
00:00:49,188 --> 00:00:53,158
Python, CadQuery and everything else SOMA needs comes included.

11
00:00:55,178 --> 00:00:57,192
The packages are not signed yet.

12
00:00:57,192 --> 00:01:00,591
On Windows, SmartScreen warns once on the first start:

13
00:01:00,591 --> 00:01:02,668
click More info, then Run anyway.

14
00:01:02,668 --> 00:01:06,508
On macOS, open the app the first time with right-click, Open.

15
00:01:07,208 --> 00:01:08,417
This is the start page.

16
00:01:08,417 --> 00:01:11,098
Your recent models are listed here, with a preview.

17
00:01:11,958 --> 00:01:12,677
New to SOMA?

18
00:01:12,677 --> 00:01:17,889
Start tutorial opens an example model and walks you through the window in twelve steps.

19
00:01:17,889 --> 00:01:18,728
Let's take it.

20
00:01:19,428 --> 00:01:22,337
A loading screen shows each step while the model is set up.

21
00:01:23,037 --> 00:01:24,666
The tour begins with the window:

22
00:01:24,666 --> 00:01:28,687
the 3D view in the middle, the agent on the right, and the sidebar on the left.

23
00:01:29,387 --> 00:01:31,920
Next is SOMA AI, the agent built into SOMA.

24
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:36,397
You tell it what you want in your own words, or show it a photo of a sketch.

25
00:01:37,097 --> 00:01:40,489
Already using Claude Code, Codex or another coding agent?

26
00:01:40,489 --> 00:01:43,227
The plus menu starts it in a terminal instead.

27
00:01:43,927 --> 00:01:46,258
The model itself is code, in model.py.

28
00:01:46,258 --> 00:01:48,344
You don't have to read or edit it:

29
00:01:48,344 --> 00:01:50,920
telling the agent what you want is enough.

30
00:01:51,620 --> 00:01:55,597
The tour goes on with measuring, mark up, parameters, history and export.

31
00:01:55,597 --> 00:01:57,830
We skip ahead and see them all in action.

32
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:02,468
SOMA AI is the first tab of the agent area.

33
00:02:02,468 --> 00:02:05,461
The first time, it asks for a sign-in:

34
00:02:05,461 --> 00:02:11,370
your ChatGPT plan, or an API key from Anthropic, OpenAI, Google and others.

35
00:02:12,314 --> 00:02:15,539
Before the first message, a short note names the risks.

36
00:02:15,539 --> 00:02:20,524
SOMA AI works inside the model's folder, and asks before it does anything outside it.

37
00:02:21,224 --> 00:02:24,689
The model menu picks the AI model it thinks with.

38
00:02:24,689 --> 00:02:26,740
The search finds one quickly.

39
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:28,154
We take GPT-6.1 Sol.

40
00:02:28,904 --> 00:02:34,314
Settings, SOMA AI shows your sign-ins, the model, and what a conversation has used so far.

41
00:02:35,564 --> 00:02:37,542
Now just describe what you need.

42
00:02:37,542 --> 00:02:38,964
We ask for a bookshelf:

43
00:02:38,964 --> 00:02:46,877
80 centimeters wide, 180 tall and 30 deep, from 18 millimeter plywood, with open shelves at the top and two doors at the bottom.

44
00:02:49,464 --> 00:02:54,161
Before it starts, SOMA AI asks about the details it cannot guess, all at once.

45
00:02:54,161 --> 00:02:57,594
Click an answer or write your own, then send the answers.

46
00:02:58,344 --> 00:02:59,935
Then it gets to work.

47
00:02:59,935 --> 00:03:02,587
Every step shows up in plain words:

48
00:03:02,587 --> 00:03:07,210
it writes the model, builds it, and checks the result itself.

49
00:03:07,210 --> 00:03:10,544
This takes a few minutes, so we speed it up.

50
00:03:11,294 --> 00:03:12,758
And here is the bookshelf.

51
00:03:12,758 --> 00:03:16,304
Every board is a part of its own, listed in the structure tree.

52
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:17,869
Now we save it.

53
00:03:17,869 --> 00:03:24,070
SOMA packs the model folder with its full history into a single .soma file, like a CAD file you can keep and share.

54
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:28,174
To change something, you can simply show it.

55
00:03:28,174 --> 00:03:30,768
Open Mark up and draw right on the view:

56
00:03:30,768 --> 00:03:33,816
circle the spot, add an arrow and a short note.

57
00:03:34,516 --> 00:03:38,262
Send to agent puts the sketch into the message for SOMA AI.

58
00:03:38,262 --> 00:03:40,166
Add one sentence, and send it.

59
00:03:44,153 --> 00:03:46,283
And there is the drawer, right where we drew it.

60
00:03:47,220 --> 00:03:50,744
Values the agent made adjustable show up in the Parameters tab:

61
00:03:50,744 --> 00:03:54,828
the outer size, the number of compartments, the board thickness and more.

62
00:03:55,528 --> 00:03:59,487
Drag a slider or type a value, and SOMA rebuilds the model.

63
00:03:59,487 --> 00:04:03,178
The agent is not involved, and the code stays as it is.

64
00:04:03,878 --> 00:04:06,168
Reset all brings back the agent's values.

65
00:04:06,918 --> 00:04:08,917
Animations work the same way:

66
00:04:08,917 --> 00:04:09,538
just ask.

67
00:04:09,538 --> 00:04:14,088
Here, the doors should swing open, and then the drawer slides out.

68
00:04:16,738 --> 00:04:18,879
The agent writes the animation in Python.

69
00:04:18,879 --> 00:04:21,908
It shows up in the Animation tab, together with its steps.

70
00:04:22,608 --> 00:04:24,953
Press play, and it runs right in the viewer.

71
00:04:24,953 --> 00:04:26,978
Make video renders it to a video file.

72
00:04:28,771 --> 00:04:31,175
SOMA AI keeps every conversation of a model.

73
00:04:31,175 --> 00:04:34,891
The clock at the top lists them, so you can pick one up again later.

74
00:04:37,538 --> 00:04:38,404
Will it hold?

75
00:04:38,404 --> 00:04:39,003
Just ask:

76
00:04:39,003 --> 00:04:41,268
how much weight can a shelf carry?

77
00:04:42,238 --> 00:04:47,024
SOMA AI sets up a load case and runs a strength analysis with the finite element method.

78
00:04:47,024 --> 00:04:50,288
CalculiX comes with SOMA, so this runs on your own computer.

79
00:04:51,038 --> 00:04:53,031
The result opens in the Analysis tab:

80
00:04:53,031 --> 00:04:55,886
the safety factor and the stress, right on the model.

81
00:04:57,338 --> 00:04:59,788
A section cuts the model open, to look inside.

82
00:05:03,771 --> 00:05:06,276
The exploded view takes the assembly apart.

83
00:05:06,276 --> 00:05:09,421
SOMA works out in which direction each part comes off.

84
00:05:11,138 --> 00:05:14,228
For the workshop, ask SOMA AI for a technical drawing.

85
00:05:16,605 --> 00:05:20,046
The Drawings tab shows every sheet next to the model.

86
00:05:20,046 --> 00:05:23,617
Drag the column wider to read the views and dimensions.

87
00:05:23,617 --> 00:05:25,695
Export saves them as PDF or DXF.

88
00:05:27,005 --> 00:05:29,281
Skills are the agent's extra knowledge.

89
00:05:29,281 --> 00:05:33,775
For a second model, a phone stand for the 3D printer, we open the Skills tab.

90
00:05:34,475 --> 00:05:36,464
Each skill has three modes.

91
00:05:36,464 --> 00:05:36,758
Off:

92
00:05:36,758 --> 00:05:38,673
the agent does not see it.

93
00:05:38,673 --> 00:05:39,410
On demand:

94
00:05:39,410 --> 00:05:42,577
the agent reads it when the topic comes up.

95
00:05:42,577 --> 00:05:43,093
Always:

96
00:05:43,093 --> 00:05:45,965
the agent follows it with every change.

97
00:05:46,665 --> 00:05:51,035
We set 3D printing to Always for this model, and enter our material and printer.

98
00:05:52,372 --> 00:05:54,230
This time we start from a picture:

99
00:05:54,230 --> 00:05:56,033
a quick sketch with measurements.

100
00:05:56,033 --> 00:05:57,782
The clip adds it to the message.

101
00:05:59,172 --> 00:06:02,662
SOMA AI reads the sketch and follows the printing rules on its own.

102
00:06:03,612 --> 00:06:06,622
A stand that is easy to print, in the material we chose.

103
00:06:07,779 --> 00:06:09,069
Finally, export:

104
00:06:09,069 --> 00:06:14,309
3MF or STL for the slicer, STEP for other CAD programs, and more.

105
00:06:15,559 --> 00:06:19,697
And if you already use a coding agent, start it from the plus menu.

106
00:06:19,697 --> 00:06:23,588
Here, Claude Code runs in a terminal, in the same model folder.

107
00:06:24,288 --> 00:06:25,358
One small change:

108
00:06:25,358 --> 00:06:27,058
paint the doors dark green.

109
00:06:30,526 --> 00:06:32,068
Same model, same history.

110
00:06:32,068 --> 00:06:33,856
Use whichever agent you like.

111
00:06:35,693 --> 00:06:36,465
That's SOMA.

112
00:06:36,465 --> 00:06:42,766
Download it for free from somacad.app, sign in to SOMA AI, and start with the part you need today.

113
00:06:42,766 --> 00:06:46,303
Press F1 in the app for the guide, or just ask SOMA AI.
